                  {
                    "id": "PRRC_kwDOAD-Lgs5DKcjN",
                    "fullDatabaseId": "1126811853",
                    "url": "https://github.com/django/django/pull/16631#discussion_r1126811853",
                    "author": {
                      "login": "David-Wobrock"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> Btw I assume any and the generator expression short-circuit, yes?\r\n\r\nYes precisely.\r\nThe logic changed slightly, it should now be more \"obvious\" when reading that the loop is only called in case the first secret doesn't match, and that it breaks out once it found one working secret.\r\n\r\n> not reintroduce a possible timing attack\r\n\r\nIt's a good point. I think that one would be able to detect which fallback secret position/number matches the given session hash.\r\nBut I don't think it is sensitive information. It informs an attacker perhaps how many/how often secret are rotated, but I'm not sure this could be leveraged directly to compromise anything 🤔 ",
                    "createdAt": "2023-03-06T17:43:19Z",
